  <h2>Most Popular Internationally-Focused Textbooks</h2>

  <p>The two most popular internationally-oriented business courses offered by community colleges are International Business (which is offered by <span data-field="ib_offering_percent">{{ ib_offering_percent }}</span> percent or <span data-field="ib_offering_count">{{ ib_offering_count }}</span> colleges as extrapolated) and International Marketing (which is offered by <span data-field="im_offering_percent">{{ im_offering_percent }}</span> percent or <span data-field="im_offering_count">{{ im_offering_count }}</span> colleges as extrapolated). The remaining internationally-oriented business courses taught (see previous page) are offered by <span data-field="other_courses_percent">{{ other_courses_percent }}</span> to <span data-field="other_courses_percent_max">{{ other_courses_percent_max }}</span> percent of the community colleges.</p>

  <p>In our 2019 benchmarking, we asked the respondents which textbooks, if any, are used in the International Business and International Marketing courses. At least <span data-field="ib_textbook_percent">{{ ib_textbook_percent }}</span> percent of the colleges used one of the identified textbooks below, in rank order (no other textbooks on these topics were used at more than 4 percent of the colleges).</p>

  <p>Interestingly, <span data-field="im_textbook_percent">{{ im_textbook_percent }}</span> percent of the respondents also said that they did not use a textbook for the International Business course. The corresponding number for the International Marketing courses was <span data-field="im_textbook_no_use_percent">{{ im_textbook_no_use_percent }}</span> percent that did not use a textbook.</p>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
